CTF Write-up: Encrypted
📝 Summary

Encrypted is a very straightforward and beginner-friendly room. It took me about 10 minutes to fully compromise the machine. The attack path involves extracting leaked credentials from an SSL certificate for initial access, followed by exploiting a recent kernel vulnerability (DirtyClone / CVE-2026-43503) to escalate privileges to root.
🔍 Enumeration

I started the box with a standard port scan, which revealed two open ports:

    Port 22: SSH

    Port 443: HTTPS

While investigating the web server on port 443, I inspected the SSL/TLS certificate details. Often, developers leave sensitive information in the certificate fields. In this case, I found a hardcoded set of credentials hidden inside the certificate:
Credentials found: iot:Goat123!
💻 Initial Access (User)

With a valid username and password in hand, I immediately connected to the target machine via SSH:
Bash

ssh iot@<TARGET_IP>
# Password: Goat123!

The login was successful, granting me access as the iot user, where I was able to read the user.txt flag.
🛡️ Privilege Escalation (Root)

Once inside the machine, I began local enumeration (I transferred linpeas.sh and pspy64 to the box to hunt for vectors). I quickly discovered that the system kernel was vulnerable to DirtyClone (CVE-2026-43503).

I downloaded the C exploit code for CVE-2026-43503 onto the target machine and compiled it using gcc:
Bash

iot@encrypt:~$ gcc -O0 -Wall -static -o DirtyClone CVE-2026-43503.c -lutil

After compiling the payload, I simply executed the resulting binary:
Bash

iot@encrypt:~$ ./DirtyClone
=== DirtyClone (CVE-2026-43503) PoC by Ashraf Zaryouh "0xBlackash" ===
[*] uid=1000 euid=1000
[+] /usr/bin/su page-cache patched successfully!
[+] Success! Spawning root shell...
#

The exploit worked flawlessly, patching the page cache for /usr/bin/su and spawning a root shell.

From there, it was just a matter of grabbing the final flag:
Bash

# cd /root
# ls
root.txt
# cat root.txt
bc06e6ee33aee532901fc6cd2926ea0789751a6bfd47f7dea5654cdf68418b85

Pwned! 🚩
